{%- comment -%}
  Quantity control for the product form.

  There was none: the PDP posted no quantity at all, so /cart/add defaulted to 1
  and a shopper who wanted three of something had to add it, open the bag, and
  step the line up twice. The buy-more ladder further down the column was
  advertising a discount the buy box had no way to reach.

  NOT [data-qty-change]. That attribute is the CART line stepper, handled by a
  delegated listener on document in theme.js that posts /cart/change with an
  absolute target quantity — reusing the name here would fire a cart mutation
  for a product that is not in the cart yet. The steppers use [data-qty-step]
  (-1 / +1) and are inert until theme.js is taught to read them.

  Without JavaScript the two step buttons do nothing, which is why the control
  is a real <input type="number" min="1">: the native spinner and the keyboard
  still work, and the value posts with the form. type="button" on the steppers
  is load-bearing — a bare <button> inside a form submits it, so an untyped
  minus button would add to cart instead of decrementing.

  Params: section_id · min (default 1)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign qty_min = min | default: 1 -%}
{%- assign qty_id = 'pdp-qty-' | append: section_id -%}
<div class="pdp-qty" data-qty>
  <label class="pdp-qty__label lbl-sm mute" for="{{ qty_id }}">{{ 'product.form.quantity' | t }}</label>
  <div class="pdp-qty__control">
    <button type="button" class="pdp-qty__step" data-qty-step="-1" aria-controls="{{ qty_id }}" aria-label="{{ 'product.form.quantity_decrease' | t }}">
      <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14"/></svg>
    </button>
    <input
      id="{{ qty_id }}"
      class="pdp-qty__input"
      type="number"
      name="quantity"
      value="{{ qty_min }}"
      min="{{ qty_min }}"
      step="1"
      inputmode="numeric"
      autocomplete="off"
      data-qty-input
    >
    <button type="button" class="pdp-qty__step" data-qty-step="1" aria-controls="{{ qty_id }}" aria-label="{{ 'product.form.quantity_increase' | t }}">
      <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
    </button>
  </div>
</div>
